---
onetaskgraph_template: 1
description: >-
  The tail of the planning workflow, for a plan already drafted or edited since: the spikes
  whose definitions changed, the spike evidence, check, review, design document, copy onto
  the board, and the user's approval. `just finish-plan
  <plan>` creates it and launches it in one flow.
variables:
  plan:
    description: The qualified id of the plan project the planner writes, `authoring:<native id>`, from the brief's `Plan project:` line.
    type: text
    required: true
  native:
    description: The plan project's native id, the part of `plan` after its source.
    type: text
    required: true
  plan_title:
    description: The plan's title, as the plan store holds it, which the approval question quotes.
    type: text
    required: true
  brief_text:
    description: What the plan was briefed to do, for the design document's What and Why; the plan's own description when no brief is at hand.
    type: text
    required: true
  destination:
    description: The configured source the reviewed plan and its design document are copied into.
    type: text
    default: plans
members:
  - id: "{{ native }}-finishing-spikes"
    title: "Run the spikes of {{ plan }} whose definitions changed"
    template: {file: step.md.j2}
    answers:
      description: "`scripts/spike-records.sh run` runs the spikes of `{{ plan }}-spikes` whose definitions changed since they last ran, attached in this flow, and settles done at once when there are none."
    metadata:
      onepipeline.id: spikes
      onepipeline.kind: command
      onepipeline.command: [scripts/spike-records.sh, run, "{{ plan }}"]
  - id: "{{ native }}-finishing-spike-evidence"
    title: "Record the spike evidence of {{ plan }}"
    template: {file: step.md.j2}
    answers:
      description: "`scripts/spike-records.sh record` records, on each task built on spikes, the spike definitions its evidence now reflects."
    depends_on: ["{{ native }}-finishing-spikes"]
    metadata:
      onepipeline.id: spike-evidence
      onepipeline.kind: command
      onepipeline.command: [scripts/spike-records.sh, record, "{{ plan }}"]
  - id: "{{ native }}-finishing-check"
    title: "Check {{ plan }} as its launch will load it"
    template: {file: step.md.j2}
    answers:
      description: "`onepipeline plan check` over the plan, with this host's install check and spike-evidence check registered."
    depends_on: ["{{ native }}-finishing-spike-evidence"]
    metadata:
      onepipeline.id: check
      onepipeline.kind: command
      onepipeline.command: [env, "ORCHESTRATOR_PLAN={{ plan }}", scripts/onepipeline.sh, plan, check, "{{ plan }}", --check, orchestrator/host_adoption_check.py, --check, scripts/spike-evidence-check.sh]
  - id: "{{ native }}-finishing-review"
    title: "Review {{ plan }}"
    template: {file: step.md.j2}
    answers:
      description: "`scripts/review-plan-item.sh` judges every unreviewed task and the project, and attests each pass."
    depends_on: ["{{ native }}-finishing-check"]
    metadata:
      onepipeline.id: review
      onepipeline.kind: command
      onepipeline.command: [scripts/review-plan-item.sh, "{{ plan }}"]
  - id: "{{ native }}-finishing-design"
    title: "Write the design document of {{ plan }}"
    template: {file: design.md.j2}
    answers:
      plan: "{{ plan }}"
      native: "{{ native }}"
      brief_text: "{{ brief_text }}"
    depends_on: ["{{ native }}-finishing-review"]
    metadata:
      onepipeline.id: design
      onepipeline.persona: ../personas/design-doc.yaml
      onepipeline.agent_graph: graphs/design-doc.yaml
  - id: "{{ native }}-finishing-copy"
    title: "Copy {{ plan }} and its documents to {{ destination }}"
    template: {file: step.md.j2}
    answers:
      description: "`just copy-plan` copies the plan, its tasks and its documents into `{{ destination }}`, and publishes the board copy's location of the design document as the step output `design_url`."
    depends_on: ["{{ native }}-finishing-design"]
    metadata:
      onepipeline.id: copy
      onepipeline.kind: command
      onepipeline.command: [just, copy-plan, "{{ plan }}", "{{ destination }}"]
  - id: "{{ native }}-finishing-approve-design"
    title: "Approve the design of {{ plan }}"
    template: {file: step.md.j2}
    answers:
      description: "Waits for the user's approval of the design document on the board copy."
    depends_on: ["{{ native }}-finishing-copy"]
    metadata:
      onepipeline.id: approve-design
      onepipeline.kind: human
      onepipeline.human_item:
        kind: question
        priority: medium
        title: >-
          Approve the design "{{ plan_title }}" or suggest changes
        body: >-
          [Read the design document](${steps.copy.design_url}) for "{{ plan_title }}".
          Choose Approve if it is right, or write the changes you want.
        choices:
          - id: approve
            title: Approve
            description: The design is right as written, and the plan may run.
---
The finishing run of `{{ plan }}`: changed spikes, spike evidence, check, review, design document, copy to `{{ destination }}`, and the user's approval.
